{"questions":[{"question_id":"HPHBaKmlxkL74LLK","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"rotational-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"combined-translational-and-rotational-motion","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"two-solid-cylinders-p-and-q-of-same-mass-and-same-radius-sta-2012-marks-4-hphbakmlxkl74llk.htm","content":"Two solid cylinders P and Q of same mass and same radius start rolling down a fixed inclined\nplane from the same height at the same time. Cylinder P has most of its mass concentrated near\nits surface, while Q has most of its mass concentrated near the axis. Which statement(s) is(are)\ncorrect?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both cylinders P and Q reach the ground at the same time."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Cylinders P has larger linear acceleration than cylinder Q."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both cylinders reach the ground with same translational kinetic energy."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Cylinder Q reaches the ground with larger angular speed."}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>Since Cylinder P has most of its mass concentrated near its surface, its moment of inertia (about the cylinder axis) is greater than that of Cylinder Q, i.e., <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.65ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.85ex\" height=\"2.195ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 3469.9 970.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(473,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1331.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2387.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(473,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The forces acting on the cylinder include its weight <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.072ex\" height=\"1.464ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 1358 647\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(878,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the normal reaction <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.009ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 888 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, and the frictional force <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.244ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 550 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-wid